# type 1031). Libraries built with a recent NDK for API 29+ use ELF TLS, which
# on arm64 means TLSDESC; Klepton's loader refused the relocation and the
# library with it (Meta's Interaction SDK in dozens of titles, Meta body
# tracking, ...). The descriptor's resolver answers the variable's offset from
# the thread pointer the guest reads (TPIDRRO_EL0 — Klepton rewrites guest
# reads of TPIDR_EL0 to it): each thread gets its own copy of the library's TLS
# block on first use, initialised from PT_TLS.
