# ANGLE's context is ES 3.0 (no compute); Unreal enables compute from the ES
# level and treats a failed compute link as fatal (FailedComputeProgramLink),
# then crashes. A compute shader becomes a trivial vertex shader that brings a
# trivial fragment shader when attached, so the program links and dispatches do
# nothing (GPU-compute effects are missing). Unreal only: Unity falls back from
# an invalid kernel, and a "valid" one writing nothing would be worse there.
