# 43 — secondary command buffers replayed outside a render pass. MoltenVK
# (v1.4.2) replays a secondary's commands through the primary's encoder; a draw
# there restarts the Metal render pass from the primary's current render pass,
# and with none open (the primary never began one, or already ended it — invalid
# Vulkan that a mobile driver tolerates) it dereferences a NULL subpass and the
# process faults on the first frame. Begin/end of render passes and dynamic
# rendering are now tracked per command buffer, and vkCmdExecuteCommands drops
# secondaries recorded to continue a render pass when the primary has none
# open: those draws are lost, the frame is not. Each such call is logged (the
# first 24) with the render pass the secondary expected. KL_VK_SEC_GUARD=0 logs
# without dropping.
