# only a file's video track (getTrackCount answered 1), so a title playing an
# MP4 with a stereo AAC soundtrack through Unity's VideoPlayer showed the
# picture and never made a sound. The file's first AAC track is now a second
# track: its format carries mime audio/mp4a-latm, sample-rate, channel-count,
# durationUs, max-input-size, language and csd-0 (the AudioSpecificConfig,
# read from the track's esds cookie or built from the stream description).
# Samples are compressed AAC access units, one per packet, read with a second
# AVAssetReader (nil output settings), and the extractor interleaves the
# selected tracks by timestamp as Android does: selectTrack builds the set
# (nothing selected still means the video track alone, as before), the sample
# calls answer for the earliest selected sample, advance moves only that
# track, seekTo moves both. AMediaCodec "audio/mp4a-latm" is an AudioConverter
# (AAC -> 16-bit interleaved PCM) configured from csd-0, on the same input and
# output buffer model as the video codec; its output buffers are CPU-readable,
# it reports OUTPUT_FORMAT_CHANGED (audio/raw, sample-rate, channel-count,
# pcm-encoding 2) ahead of the first one, and end of stream comes back as an
# empty buffer flagged EOS. The decoded PCM then goes wherever the title's
# own audio mixer sends it. A file with no AAC track is unchanged (one track).
# MV_VIDEO_AUDIO=0 turns all of it off.
python3 - "$K/runtime/media" <<'PYEOF'
import sys
d = sys.argv[1]
