# 77 — the APK's signing certificate. A native library that checks it was not
# re-signed goes ActivityThread -> Application -> PackageManager, asks
# getPackageInfo(<own package>, GET_SIGNATURES) and reads PackageInfo.signatures.
# Nothing answered that field, so the guest got null, called
# Signature.toCharsString() on it and crashed in strlen(NULL). The field is now
# a one-element Signature[] holding the title's own signing certificate:
# toCharsString (lowercase hex of the DER, Android's format), toChars,
# toByteArray, hashCode (Arrays.hashCode of the DER) and equals; signingInfo /
# SigningInfo.getApkContentsSigners answer the same array for the newer API.
