# constants. Several calls the catalogue makes had no host implementation:
#  - java.io.File(File, String), canRead, canWrite and FileOutputStream
#    (open, write, close): a title that writes its own file got nothing back and
#    the bytes went nowhere. File gains its constructors and the usual queries
#    (exists, isDirectory, isFile, length, lastModified, getName, mkdir(s),
#    delete, space) and FileOutputStream writes for real, both on the host
#    path the runtime's guest-path mapping gives (kl_guest_path: /sdcard and
#    the files directories land in the app container, as getFilesDir does).
#  - com.unity3d.player.DeviceInfo, which Unity's Java answers from Build,
#    Locale and the clock: the same Build.MODEL / VERSION.RELEASE and locale
#    the runtime already reports elsewhere, the boot time from the clocks and
#    the cache volume's size in KiB, as Unity computes it.
#  - UnityPermissions.requestUserPermissions: each permission is decided by the
#    manifest model (klj_permission_state) and the callback proxy, when there
#    is one, is told the result the way Unity's Java does. Before Unity 2023
#    the interface is onPermissionGranted/onPermissionDenied(String) (Unity's
#    Java reports a denial as onPermissionDenied on API 30+, and the presented
#    API is 32); from 2023 on it is onPermissionResult(String[], int[]) with
